       ],
       "cap": "In units with $\\hbar = 1$, in which (6.24) is written."
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{L}{i\\frac{d}{d\\kt}|\\kpsi\\rangle} = \\mk{R}{\\left(\\kDelta - \\frac{i\\kgamma}{2}\\right)|2\\rangle\\langle 2|\\kpsi\\rangle}",
       "uses": [
        1
       ],
       "cap": "$\\hat{c}^\\dagger\\hat{c} = |2\\rangle\\langle 2|$."
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{L}{\\frac{d}{d\\kt}|\\kpsi\\rangle} = \\mk{R}{-\\left(\\frac{\\kgamma}{2} + i\\kDelta\\right)|2\\rangle\\langle 2|\\kpsi\\rangle}",
       "uses": [],
       "cap": "Dividing by $i$: $-i(\\Delta - i\\gamma/2) = -(\\gamma/2 + i\\Delta)$."
      }
     ],
     "num": "(6.25)",
     "note": "The book prints the right side as $-\\left(\\frac{\\kgamma}{2} + i\\kDelta\\right)|2\\rangle$, without $\\langle 2|\\kpsi\\rangle$, the amplitude it acts on, and (6.24) with $+\\frac{i\\kgamma}{2}\\hat{c}^\\dagger\\hat{c}$; the minus sign of (6.7) is what makes the amplitude of $|2\\rangle$ decay."
